; Corn pile. Tile 4 of the tile table (84F0 + 8 * 4 = 8510) holds the pile in its rows 3-6, bytes 8513-8516.
; In chuckie.gfx the pile is two yellows, 70=EFCE00 and 71=FFFF00, and the pixels between the dots are coloured
; too (Spec256 draws a filled triangle), so each pixel gets a colour word: Spec256 index 0 is no colour and
; stays 8000 (the Spectrum paper colour). One byte per line, leftmost pixel first.
; Pile bitmap (set bits), one byte per line:
; 8513 ...#....
; 8514 ..#.#...
; 8515 .#.#.#..
; 8516 #.#.#.#.
